  "body": "## What changed\n\nA new count, `iso::unpaired_edges`, sits beside `open_edges`. After the same 1e-9 weld, it counts the edges that are not on exactly two facets. A facet whose corners meet at the weld leaves an edge from a corner to itself, and that edge always counts. The two places that read \"the mesh is closed\" now use it:\n\n- `iso::extract_with`: a dual mesh with any such edge is not returned; the marching mesh of the same samples stands in, as it already did for an odd edge. The warning says \"edges not on two facets\".\n- `app::stock_export::machined_mesh`: a mesh with any such edge is refused, not written. The message reads \"… edges not on two facets - refused, not written\". The module's law \"A hole is a refusal\" names fins as well as holes.\n\n`open_edges` is unchanged (odd edges only) and stays for its other callers, all of them tests that use it as their closed check.\n\nThe two counts and their unit tests live in a new child file, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/iso_edges.rs`. The merge with main brought the #4107 tests into `iso.rs` (408 lines, over the 400-line rule), so the counts moved out along the extraction / checking seam. `iso` re-exports both, so every caller and test path is the same.\n\n## Readings\n\nFrom the issue, measured on main `a1c57b4` (before #4107 merged): 937 tests passed (all `camcraft-sim` tests and the `camcraft-app` suites `stock_export`, `contour_stock_run` and `stepped_stock_rapid`). 20 meshes reached the two sites:\n\n| Site | Meshes | Odd edges > 0 | Edges on 3+ facets > 0 | Collapsed facets > 0 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| dual (in `extract_with`) | 11 | 0 | 1 | 0 |\n| marching | 5 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| `stock_export` | 4 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\nSo the one behaviour change in the current suites is the dual mesh of a cube smaller than a cell (`stock_dual::a_body_under_one_cell_never_panics_and_never_opens`): 6 facets, volume 0, three flat fins on one edge. It is now refused, and the marching mesh stands in: 24 facets, every edge on two facets, volume 5.19e-3.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nSynthetic shapes only. No new test binary:\n- `stock_dual::a_body_under_one_cell_never_panics_and_never_opens` (existing suite, whose gate map covers `stock_sim::iso`) now also asserts `unpaired_edges == 0` for both methods. With `extract_with` put back on `open_edges` it fails: `Dual: every edge on two facets`, left 1, right 0.\n- Unit tests in `iso_edges.rs`:\n  - `two_cubes_on_one_edge_pass_open_edges_and_count_as_unpaired`: two unit cubes sharing one edge; `open_edges` is 0 and `unpaired_edges` is 1.\n  - `a_facet_collapsed_at_the_weld_counts_as_unpaired`: a cube plus two facets whose first two corners meet at the weld and whose third corners are apart. Every edge, the edge from the welded corner to itself included, is on two facets, so `open_edges` is 0 and `unpaired_edges` is 1. Without the corner-to-itself rule it fails: left 0, right 1.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the final head `8876f6072` (the review fix to the collapsed-facet pin and the provenance line, on `301118823`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 86 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 22.7 min.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nOn `301118823` (upstream/main `de035b4` merged in, the split into `iso_edges.rs` on top):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 86 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 16.7 min. The new file maps to the whole `stock_sim` module (82 suites), so every sim suite and the app suites that read stock simulation ran.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nOn the first head `825d9c193` (base `a1c57b4`; the merge changed `iso.rs` only by adding #4107's crossing and tests):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 7.7 min.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: green, 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 54.3 min (most of it the release build, on a shared box). It was not rerun on the final head.\n\nMain has moved since `de035b4`; none of the later commits touch the changed files.\n\n- No heavy step: this is not a `P1` (work-issue section 3).\n\nThe decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/4122-solid-edges.md`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No test reaches the `stock_export` refusal through a mesh that only the new count refuses; the 4 export meshes measured above all pass both counts. The change there is the count it calls.\n- The heavy lanes.\n- The GUI (the viewer's mesh cache reads `machined_mesh`).\n- Edge orientation (each edge used once in each direction) is not checked; fins pass it, so the count is the check that catches them (see the decision file).\n\nEffort: high (stock simulation is under the safety floor).\nChangelog: Stock simulation: the closed-mesh check now refuses an edge on four or more facets, not only an odd one; a dual mesh of fins falls back to marching tetrahedra, and the stock export no longer writes such a mesh as a solid.\n\nBranch: upstream/main merged in (plain merge); the diff is 5 files: `iso.rs`, `iso_edges.rs`, `stock_export.rs`, `stock_dual.rs` and the decision file.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4122\n",
